    "diversity_note": "China is home to 56 officially recognized ethnic groups and extensive linguistic diversity. The Ministry of Education describes multiple language families, regional Sinitic varieties, and minority languages. A language family, language, and dialect/variety must not be conflated.",
    "classification_note": "Some Sinitic varieties traditionally called fangyan are not mutually intelligible. LWT separates each selected language/group and attaches a local profile focus (for example Hong Kong Cantonese, Shanghai Wu, Meixian Hakka, Xiangxiang, Nanchang Gan and Zhangzhou Southern Min). These profiles do not claim to cover every variety in a code group."
